Fri Nov 20 17:34:01 UTC 2026 - Fridrich Strba <fstrba@suse.com>

- Upgrade to version 5.5
  * Notable changes
    + Improved connection and async IOSession pool implementations
    + HTTP/2: RFC 9113/7541 conformance, rapid reset and control
      frame overhead protection, limit on pending requests per
      connection
    + Added QUERY method, Structured Field Values (RFC 9651) and
      Digest Fields (RFC 9530) support
    + SSLContexts respect SSL/TLS system properties by default
    + Fixed premature termination of incomplete chunked messages
      in the classic transport

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Aug 13 15:05:00 UTC 2026 - Fridrich Strba <fstrba@suse.com>

- Upgrade to version 5.4.3
  * Notable changes in the 5.4.x series:
    + Security: Sets finite defaults for incoming HTTP/1 messages
      to mitigate Denial of Service (DoS) header attacks by setting
      a maximum line length of 8,192 bytes and maximum header
      count of 100 by default.
    + RFC Conformance: Support for RFC 9218 (Extensible Prioritization
      Scheme for HTTP) and improved compliance to RFC 9113 (HTTP/2).
    + Sockets: Support for Unix domain sockets for both classic
      and asynchronous transports.
    + Connection Pool: Introduced experimental OFFLOCK lock-free,
      route-segmented connection pool (RouteSegmentedConnPool).
    + Redesigned the classic over async API bridge.
    + Default 5-second TCP keep-alive enabled by default to
      optimize connection reuse.
    + Fixed regression in backpressure handling of async TLS
      sessions.
    + Fixed a deadlock in LaxConnPool where expired connection
      cleanup failed to update the number of available connections.
    + Corrected a latency regression in async transport where
      TCP_NODELAY failed to be set correctly.
    + Fixed a memory leak in the HTTP/2 stream priority.

